# dialog draws the gauge as one reversible (fg,bg) pair: the unfilled trough uses
# it as-is (fg on bg), the filled portion swaps it (bg becomes the fill color, fg
# becomes the text drawn over that fill). That forces trough-text and fill-bg to
# share one slot, and trough-bg and fill-text to share the other — "always white
# text + dark track + magenta fill" needs 3 independent colors, dialog only gives
# 2. Picked full contrast + a dark track over keeping magenta in the gauge:
# trough = white text on black (matches the rest of the dark theme), filled
# portion = black text on white (loses the brand accent here, but never a
# contrast problem in either state).
gauge_color              = (WHITE,BLACK,ON)
